PRETABLE -- #529 kill table 6 (TARGETED), written BEFORE the table (mtime is the order proof)
Instrument: regress/crime_width_probe.py after REPAIR 7, frozen by the driver as crime_width_probe.table6.py -- 121 rows
(87 row() call sites; no row added or removed since table 5's instrument).  First measurement (L1): ../probe_first9_fix.out
on the FIXED build (the driver's BASE run is the second).

THE ONE CHANGE, and the finding that bought it.  The Opus second-closing seat MEASURED a decline answering the ADDRESSED
LANES of the register at CRIME_INTSTAT -- `odata = d->reg[relative_addr / 8] >> (8 * (8 - len - (relative_addr & 7)))',
the lane the model's own 4-byte read path uses -- at 111/111 AND at 121/121 on repair 6 (its batch3/probe121_istat_lane.raw):
a refused read at the label names bytes 0-1, and repair 6's seed 0x10000001 was nonzero only in byte 7.  Repair 7 seeds
SOFTINT and INTMASK with 0x0101000010000001 (bytes 0, 1 and 7 nonzero; bit 28 kept for the reassert), and the header
discloses the same lane form at REV, CONTROL and TIME as EQUIVALENT (the model holds bytes 0-1 at 0 there).

WARRANT FOR TARGETING, by the tables' rule.  CHANGED sessions: imask, istat, gate (all use BIT).  Every other session's
command list is byte-identical to table 5's instrument.  RE-RUN (every table-5-predicted red row in those sessions):
imaskft a_istat istat2 imask2 istatsh h_imask istat_od1 c2_lbl_imask c2_lbl_istat c2_reg_imask c2_reg_istat c2_land_or
c2_pre_irq o_hi_gate o_pa_gate.  STANDING (a red row outside those sessions): o_rearm4 (rearm once), p_rd_lh_all, and
every other table-5 kill.  Table 5 is still measuring repair 6 as this is written; its results stand for repair 6, and
this table re-measures only what repair 7 can move.

LANES: three, table 5's warrant.  Table 5's remaining lanes may still be running beside these; the oracles count steps.

CHANNEL -- per mutant, predicted red rows on the repair-7 instrument (121 rows; CONTROL=OK throughout)
  base            none (121/121)
  imaskft         imask lb, imask sb, imask lh, imask sh                                              -- 117/121
  a_istat         istat lb, istat sb, istat lh, istat sh                                              -- 117/121
  istat2 / imask2 / h_imask   istat lh, sh / imask lh, sh / imask lh, sh                             -- 119/121 each
  istatsh         istat sh                                                                            -- 120/121
  istat_od1       istat lb v0, istat lh v0                                                            -- 119/121
  c2_lbl_imask    imask once (2)          c2_lbl_istat   istat once (2)                               -- 120/121 each
  c2_reg_imask    imask lb v0, imask lh v0 (the whole-register answer: low bytes 0x01 / 0x0001)       -- 119/121
  c2_reg_istat    istat lb v0, istat lh v0                                                            -- 119/121
  c2_land_or      imask keeps (0x010100001000ffff)                                                    -- 120/121
  c2_pre_irq      imask once (0), istat once (0)                                                      -- 119/121
  o_hi_gate, o_pa_gate   gate run (the line is still asserted: INTMASK and SOFTINT share the seed)   -- 120/121 each
  q_istat_leak    istat lb v0, istat lh v0 (the Opus seat's whole-register form)                      -- 119/121
  q_istat_lane    istat lb v0 (byte 0 = 0x01), istat lh v0 (bytes 0-1 = 0x0101)                       -- 119/121
  q_dog_leak      dog v0 (0xef), dog lh v0 (0xcdef) -- both sign-extended                             -- 119/121
  l_imask         imask lb v0 (0x01), imask lh v0 (0x0101)                                            -- 119/121
  l_dog           dog v0 (0x01), dog lh v0 (0x0123)                                                   -- 119/121
  l_rev, l_ctl, l_time   none -- PREDICTED EQUIVALENT, disclosed: bytes 0-1 of REV (0x11), CONTROL (0x100) and
                  TIME (kept to 32 bits) are 0                                                        -- 121/121 each

